Config/benchmark/defaults:
    The benchmark Rmd defaults to run_benchmark = TRUE, force_refit = FALSE,
    n_cores = 9, cohort_transition_version = "contextual",
    cohort_contextual_apply_to = "all",
    cohort_context_keep_baseline_when_sparse = FALSE,
    cohort_context_lambda_sparse_unknown = 0.10, and run_nn_holdout = TRUE.
Config/benchmark/behavior:
    The command loads the current checkout with pkgload::load_all(), so it uses
    this repository's source code rather than an already installed alfakR
    package. Existing complete and version-compatible fit outputs are reused;
    missing or incompatible outputs are run. For cohort_transition/contextual
    outputs, cache compatibility requires both cohort_transition_version and
    cohort_contextual_apply_to to match the requested benchmark settings.
    Regular nn_prior tasks are parallelized with n_cores.
    cohort_transition/contextual first learns one cohort prior per pm x minobs
    group, then parallelizes per-patient contextual refits with the same n_cores
    value on Unix platforms.
Config/benchmark/output:
    The default HTML report is written next to
    benchmark/scr/run_benchmark_alfak.Rmd. Fit outputs are written under
    benchmark/results/fits.
